39 0 obj
<<
/ActualText (Three event-study plots of WATT estimates for Walmart openings. Panels &#x00028;a&#x00029; and &#x00028;b&#x00029;, using CS &#x00028;2021&#x00029; and rolling IPWRA with demeaning, show upward pre-trends. Panel &#x00028;c&#x00029;, using rolling IPWRA with detrending, addresses these pre-trends. The figure compares three sets of WATT estimates for the effect of Walmart openings on log retail employment. Panel &#x00028;a&#x00029; reports estimates from the CS &#x00028;2021&#x00029; approach, and Panel &#x00028;b&#x00029; reports rolling IPWRA estimates with demeaning. Both panels display upward pre-treatment trends, suggesting that the corresponding post-treatment estimates may partly reflect pre-existing differential trends rather than only treatment effects. Panel &#x00028;c&#x00029; reports rolling IPWRA estimates with detrending. After detrending, the pre-treatment estimates no longer show an upward trend, making the post-treatment estimates more readily interpretable as treatment-effect estimates.)
/A 358 0 R
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/S /Figure
/T ()
/Pg 21 0 R
/Alt (Three event-study plots of WATT estimates for Walmart openings. Panels &#x00028;a&#x00029; and &#x00028;b&#x00029;, using CS &#x00028;2021&#x00029; and rolling IPWRA with demeaning, show upward pre-trends. Panel &#x00028;c&#x00029;, using rolling IPWRA with detrending, addresses these pre-trends. The figure compares three sets of WATT estimates for the effect of Walmart openings on log retail employment. Panel &#x00028;a&#x00029; reports estimates from the CS &#x00028;2021&#x00029; approach, and Panel &#x00028;b&#x00029; reports rolling IPWRA estimates with demeaning. Both panels display upward pre-treatment trends, suggesting that the corresponding post-treatment estimates may partly reflect pre-existing differential trends rather than only treatment effects. Panel &#x00028;c&#x00029; reports rolling IPWRA estimates with detrending. After detrending, the pre-treatment estimates no longer show an upward trend, making the post-treatment estimates more readily interpretable as treatment-effect estimates.)
>>
endobj
